<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toltén River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Toltén River flows from Lake Villarrica about 120 kilometres west to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> in the Araucanía region of southern Chile. In colonial times the lands between the Biobío and the Toltén formed the core of the independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> territory. The Spanish town of Villarrica, near its source, was destroyed in the great Mapuche rising of 1598–1604.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tolten-river.jpg" alt="Toltén River" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iain and Sarah · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Villarrica_town_and_volcano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
